# `FLOWCHART-ROLE-KEYWORDS` / `GENRE-NAMESPACE` `GENRE-NAMESPACE`: `process`, `decision` and `terminator` belong to the
# `flowchart` keyword namespace and to no other. The header genre's allowlist
# is what enforces it — no per-keyword code — so the diagnostic is the same
# "not allowed in genre X" a scene keyword gets inside `bitfield`. Multi-
# section (`MULTI-FIGURE-DOCUMENTS`): one file, four headers, four allowlists.
figdown 0.1 block
decision q "Header valid?"
figdown 0.1 topology
process p "Forward"
figdown 0.1 bitfield
terminator t "Done"
figdown 0.1 flowchart
decision q "Header valid?"
